<title>USA: Procter &amp; Gamble settles infringement suit.</title>
<headline>Procter &amp; Gamble settles infringement suit.</headline>
<dateline>CINCINNATI, Ohio 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Procter &amp; Gamble Co said Tuesday its infringement lawsuit against TRISTAR Corp had been settled.</p>
<p>Procter &amp; Gamble said the lawsuit was filed last November to stop TRISTAR from selling its Everscent High Performance deoderant products.</p>
<p>Under the settlement, TRISTAR agreed to change the labeling of its Everscent High Performance deodorant products and acknowledged that Procter &amp; Gamble's trademarks and package design rights for its Old Spice brand are proprietary and distinctive, Procter &amp; Gamble said.</p>
<p>The company said TRISTAR will also pay monetary damages of an undisclosed amount.</p>
